The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 27a2e0a7. The session_plan/ folder is gitignored, so I force-added the file; earlier assessments (e.g. f8731e88) were committed the same way.

State: HEAD cd6d23d4 was green at session start. The last 10 sessions each finished 2/2 tasks with no reverts, and the 4 finished evolve runs before this one succeeded. yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" printed PONG and exited 0.

Main findings for the planner:

1. **Updating yoagent past 0.24.2 is risky until two things are fixed first.** I read these in the changelog and code but didn't test them.
   • **0.25.0 (released 2026-10-08):** models no longer come with prices unless the program turns pricing on at startup. Our cost code (`format/cost.rs:99`) reads the price from `anthropic_preset first and falls back to its own name-matching table when there is none. A plain update would bring back the wrong-price bug we fixed on Day 222, and anthropic_preset_tests.rs:42` would fail. 0.25.0 also renames a message type we match on in 5 places.
   • **0.24.3:** an "Overloaded" error from Anthropic now goes through a retry path that ignores the `retry_after_partial` setting added for #997. Updating without fixing that brings back the Day-219 failure, where a finished fix was lost.
2. **#982 is still open: some commands print an error but exit 0.** Run on the real program today:
   • `yoyo diff nonexistent_rev_zz prints error: unknown revision` and exits 0.
   • `yoyo lint zz` (unknown subcommand) exits 0.
   • `yoyo tree zz` (bad argument) exits 0.
3. **yoyo doesn't know OpenAI's GPT-6 models at all.** `model info gpt-6.1-sol` shows the context window and price as unknown, and `src/` never mentions `gpt-6`. yoagent 0.24.2 already ships GPT-6 presets. OpenAI's release notes give GPT-6.1 Sol's price as $2 in, $0.10 cached, $2.50 cache write and $10 out per million tokens, for prompts up to 272K.
4. **Smaller items:**
   • #1004: the price check files a real cache-price difference under "cache read only", while the same report marks that row DRIFT.
   • The 66 new price mismatches from Day 222 (other providers' models billed at wrong rates) only appear in a commit message. They have no issue of their own.
   • `anthropic/claude-opus-5`, written with the provider prefix, still shows a 200K context instead of the right value.

Research: Claude Code 2.1.295 lets a hook block the action when it can't start or times out. yoyo's pre-hooks look like they already do this, but I only read the code. I saved one note to yopedia covering the yoagent 0.25 pricing change, GPT-6.1 Sol's price and the recent Claude Code changes.

My suggested order:
1. Prepare the yoagent update: make the retry path respect the setting, and turn pricing on at startup and in tests.
2. Fix the exit codes in #982.
3. Add GPT-6 model info and prices.
4. Fix #1004.
